    "id": "aoc-2025-2",
    "year": 2025,
    "day": 2,
    "title": "Gift Shop",
    "dir": "aoc/2025/day02",
    "src": "-- AoC 2025 day 2: Gift Shop\n-- Find invalid product IDs made of a digit sequence repeated at least twice.\n--\n-- Pipeline overview (4 ticks from input comet to running totals):\n--   Tick t    : `a` and `b` parse the range endpoints from \"lo-hi\".\n--   Tick t + 1: `lo`/`hi` and `olo`/`ohi` clamp the range to even/odd digit\n--               lengths, and `step*` pick the repunit multiplier for that length.\n--   Tick t + 2: `first*`/`last*`/`span*` find the first and last multiples of\n--               each multiplier inside the clamped range.\n--   Tick t + 3: `part1`, `rep35`, `rep610`, and `repodd` add the arithmetic\n--               series sum (first + last) * count / 2 for their multiples.\n--   Tick N + 4: `shop` prints the final totals after the last range finishes.\n\nsky from 1 to comets + 4\n\n-- Stage 1: parse \"a-b\" from this tick's comet.\nplanet a orbits 1 { digits of comet }\nplanet b orbits 1 { digits of comet after \"-\" }\n\n-- Stage 2a (even digit lengths: 2, 4, 6, 8, or 10 digits):\n-- Each input range spans at most one even digit length. If `a` has an odd\n-- number of digits, round `lo` up to the start of the next even-digit band;\n-- if `b` has an odd number of digits, round `hi` down to the end of the\n-- previous even-digit band. Initial masses (lo=10, hi=0) keep lo > hi before\n-- the first range arrives so early pipeline ticks add nothing.\nplanet lo orbits 1 mass 10 {\n  10 if a < 10\n    else 1000 if a >= 100 and a < 1000\n    else 100000 if a >= 10000 and a < 100000\n    else 10000000 if a >= 1000000 and a < 10000000\n    else 1000000000 if a >= 100000000 and a < 1000000000\n    else a\n}\n\nplanet hi orbits 1 mass 0 {\n  0 if b < 10\n    else 99 if b >= 100 and b < 1000\n    else 9999 if b >= 10000 and b < 100000\n    else 999999 if b >= 1000000 and b < 10000000\n    else 99999999 if b >= 100000000 and b < 1000000000\n    else b\n}\n\n-- A k-digit block repeated twice inside a 2k-digit band is a multiple of 10^k + 1:\n-- 2 digits -> 11, 4 -> 101, 6 -> 1001, 8 -> 10001, 10 -> 100001.\nplanet step orbits 1 mass 11 {\n  11 if a < 100\n    else 101 if a < 10000\n    else 1001 if a < 1000000\n    else 10001 if a < 100000000\n    else 100001\n}\n\n-- Part 2 also allows odd repeat counts inside even-length numbers:\n--   - 6-digit numbers repeated 3 times (ab|ab|ab) are multiples of 10101.\n--   - 10-digit numbers repeated 5 times (ab|ab|ab|ab|ab) are multiples of 101010101.\n-- For other even lengths (2, 4, 8), use 10^11 so no multiple falls in [lo, hi].\nplanet step2 orbits 1 mass 100000000000 {\n  10101 if a >= 10000 and a < 1000000\n    else 101010101 if a >= 100000000\n    else 100000000000\n}\n\n-- Numbers repeated 6 times (a|a|a|a|a|a, multiple of 111111) or 10 times\n-- (multiple of 1111111111) are counted by both `step` (2-repeat) and `step2`\n-- (3- or 5-repeat), so we track them here and subtract once by inclusion-exclusion.\nplanet step6 orbits 1 mass 100000000000 {\n  111111 if a >= 10000 and a < 1000000\n    else 1111111111 if a >= 100000000\n    else 100000000000\n}\n\n-- Stage 2b (odd digit lengths: 3, 5, 7, or 9 digits):\n-- Clamp [a, b] to the single odd-digit band it can overlap.\nplanet olo orbits 1 mass 100 {\n  100 if a < 100\n    else 10000 if a >= 1000 and a < 10000\n    else 1000000 if a >= 100000 and a < 1000000\n    else 100000000 if a >= 10000000 and a < 100000000\n    else 10000000000 if a >= 1000000000\n    else a\n}\n\nplanet ohi orbits 1 mass 0 {\n  0 if b < 100\n    else 999 if b >= 1000 and b < 10000\n    else 99999 if b >= 100000 and b < 1000000\n    else 9999999 if b >= 10000000 and b < 100000000\n    else 999999999 if b >= 1000000000\n    else b\n}\n\n-- Multipliers for odd digit lengths in Part 2:\n--   3 digits (1x3) -> 111\n--   5 digits (1x5) -> 11111\n--   7 digits (1x7) -> 1111111\n--   9 digits (3x3) -> 1001001 (also covers 1x9 = 111111111)\nplanet ostep orbits 1 mass 111 {\n  111 if a < 1000\n    else 11111 if a < 100000\n    else 1111111 if a < 10000000\n    else 1001001\n}\n\n-- Stage 3: round `lo` up (`lo + -lo % step`) and `hi` down (`hi - hi % step`)\n-- to the first and last multiples of each multiplier inside the clamped band.\n-- `span*` carries the multiplier forward one tick so Stage 4 has it in sync.\nplanet first orbits 1 mass 11 { lo + -lo % step }\nplanet last orbits 1 mass 0   { hi - hi % step }\nplanet span orbits 1 mass 11  { step }\n\nplanet first2 orbits 1 mass 11 { lo + -lo % step2 }\nplanet last2 orbits 1 mass 0   { hi - hi % step2 }\nplanet span2 orbits 1 mass 11  { step2 }\n\nplanet first6 orbits 1 mass 11 { lo + -lo % step6 }\nplanet last6 orbits 1 mass 0   { hi - hi % step6 }\nplanet span6 orbits 1 mass 11  { step6 }\n\nplanet ofirst orbits 1 mass 111 { olo + -olo % ostep }\nplanet olast orbits 1 mass 0    { ohi - ohi % ostep }\nplanet ospan orbits 1 mass 111  { ostep }\n\n-- Stage 4: when first <= last, sum all multiples first, first + span, ..., last\n-- using the arithmetic series formula: (first + last) * ((last - first) / span + 1) / 2.\nplanet part1 orbits 1 mass 0 {\n  part1 + (first + last) * ((last - first) / span + 1) / 2 if first <= last\n    else part1\n}\n\nplanet rep35 orbits 1 mass 0 {\n  rep35 + (first2 + last2) * ((last2 - first2) / span2 + 1) / 2 if first2 <= last2\n    else rep35\n}\n\nplanet rep610 orbits 1 mass 0 {\n  rep610 + (first6 + last6) * ((last6 - first6) / span6 + 1) / 2 if first6 <= last6\n    else rep610\n}\n\nplanet repodd orbits 1 mass 0 {\n  repodd + (ofirst + olast) * ((olast - ofirst) / ospan + 1) / 2 if ofirst <= olast\n    else repodd\n}\n\n-- After 4 pipeline stages, all `comets` ranges have been accumulated.\nplanet shop orbits comets + 4 {\n  say \"part 1: {part1}\"\n  say \"part 2: {part1 + rep35 - rep610 + repodd}\"\n}\n",
    "example": "11-22,95-115,998-1012,1188511880-1188511890,222220-222224,\n1698522-1698528,446443-446449,38593856-38593862,565653-565659,\n824824821-824824827,2121212118-2121212124\n\n",
    "input": "119-210,907313-1048019,7272640820-7272795557,6315717352-6315818282,42-65,2234869-2439411,1474-2883,33023-53147,1-15,6151-14081,3068-5955,65808-128089,518490556-518593948,3535333552-3535383752,7340190-7548414,547-889,34283147-34389716,44361695-44519217,607492-669180,7071078-7183353,67-115,969-1469,3636264326-3636424525,762682710-762831570,827113-906870,205757-331544,290-523,86343460-86510016,5536957-5589517,132876-197570,676083-793651,23-41,17920-31734,440069-593347\n"
